## ARTICLE V: AUTOMATIC TERMINATION & ENFORCEMENT

**5.1. Automatic Termination Upon Breach**
This License **AUTOMATICALLY TERMINATES IMMEDIATELY** without requirement of notice or cure period if You:
 - (a) Violate any provision of Article IV (Prohibited Activities);
 - (b) Are or become a Prohibited Party under Article II;
 - (c) Derive any unauthorized Financial Benefit from the Software;
 - (d) Deploy the Software in any Service Deployment configuration; or
 - (e) Otherwise breach any material term of this Agreement.

**Upon termination, You must immediately:**
 - Cease all use of the Software;
 - Delete or destroy all copies in your possession or control;
 - Remove all Derivative Works from production environments;
 - Notify all third parties to whom you provided access to cease use; and
 - Provide written certification of compliance to Licensor.

**5.2. Post-Termination Use Constitutes Willful Infringement**
**You explicitly acknowledge and agree that:**
 - (a) Any use of the Software after termination constitutes **WILLFUL COPYRIGHT INFRINGEMENT** under 17 U.S.C. § 504;
 - (b) Such willful infringement entitles Licensor to **ENHANCED STATUTORY DAMAGES of up to $150,000 per work**;
 - (c) You waive any defense that such post-termination use was unintentional or inadvertent; and
 - (d) Continued use demonstrates knowing, intentional violation with reckless disregard for Licensor's rights.

**This provision is designed to maximize statutory damages and eliminate "innocent infringement" defenses.**

**5.3. Liquidated Damages Schedule**
Due to the difficulty of calculating actual damages from unauthorized use, the parties agree to the following **liquidated damages** as a reasonable pre-estimate of harm (not a penalty):

| Violation Type | Liquidated Damages (USD) |
|---|---|
| Unauthorized Commercial Use | $100,000 per incident |
| Service Deployment (SaaS/API/etc.) | $500,000 per deployment |
| Creating Commercial Derivative Work | $500,000 per work |
| AI Training or Integration | $1,000,000 per AI model/system |
| Use by Explicitly Named Prohibited Party | $2,000,000 per incident |
| Reverse Engineering | $750,000 per incident |
| Distribution to Third Parties | $250,000 per recipient |
| Circumventing Technical Protection Measures | $500,000 per incident |
| Patent Filing on Software-Derived Inventions | $1,000,000 per application |
| Refactoring/Reimplementation to Hide Origin | $750,000 per derivative |

**Multiple violations are cumulative. Each day of continued violation constitutes a separate incident.**

**5.4. Statutory Damages Under Copyright Law**
In addition to liquidated damages, Licensor is entitled to seek **statutory damages** under **17 U.S.C. § 504(c)**:
 - (a) Standard statutory damages: **$750 to $30,000 per work infringed**;
 - (b) **Enhanced statutory damages for willful infringement: up to $150,000 per work**;
 - (c) Statutory damages are elected at Licensor's discretion in lieu of actual damages; and
 - (d) Statutory damages do NOT require proof of actual harm or financial loss.

**By using the Software, You acknowledge that statutory damages are an available remedy.**

**5.5. Disgorgement of Profits**
Licensor is entitled to **disgorgement of all profits, revenue, cost savings, and other Financial Benefits** You derived from unauthorized use, including:
 - (a) Direct revenue from products or services incorporating the Software;
 - (b) Cost savings from operational efficiencies gained through the Software;
 - (c) Investor funding, equity appreciation, or acquisition premiums attributable to the Software;
 - (d) Advertising revenue, user engagement metrics, or other indirect monetization;
 - (e) Competitive advantages quantified as market share gains or pricing power; and
 - (f) Any other economic value extraction.

**The burden is on You to prove which portions of profits are NOT attributable to the Software.**

**5.6. Injunctive Relief (No Bond Required)**
Due to the unique nature of the Software and the irreparable harm caused by unauthorized use, Licensor is entitled to:
 - (a) **Immediate preliminary and permanent injunctive relief** to halt violations;
 - (b) **Temporary restraining orders (TROs)** to prevent imminent breaches;
 - (c) **Specific performance** compelling destruction of unauthorized copies; and
 - (d) **No requirement to post bond or security** for such relief.

**You acknowledge that monetary damages alone are inadequate to remedy unauthorized use.**

**5.7. Attorney's Fees & Costs**
The prevailing party in any legal action related to this Agreement is entitled to:
